# =============================================================================
# MXL-HotGauge additions
# =============================================================================

# --- Vendored simulators -----------------------------------------------------
# Fetched by get_and_patch_*.sh, not by cloning. snipersim is 1.6 GB, 3d-ice 457 MB,
# McPAT 13 MB. Our four hand-edited 3D-ICE sources live in MXL_3DICE_fixes/ instead --
# see that directory's README before touching the 3d-ice tree.
McPAT/
snipersim/
# (3d-ice/ is already ignored above)

# --- Installer scratch -------------------------------------------------------
.mxl/

# --- Simulation output -------------------------------------------------------
# 3D-ICE runs emit hundreds of MB per study. Everything here is regenerable from
# examples/*.py; total is ~2.3 GB.
fmu_equilibrium/
fmu_equilibrium_150s/
hybrid_opt/
leakage_feedback_smoketest/
mr_cliff/
mr_cliff_25/
mr_cliff_8core/
mr_cliff_v2/
mr_clipping_study/
mr_clipping_study_55/
mr_clipping_study_65/
sink_calibration/
steady_sink_sweep/
viability_probe/
plots/
results/
simscale_hpc/
mr_compare/
examples/simscale_replication/

# --- Keep source data that the generic rules above would swallow -------------
# `*.png` is ignored as build output, but these are INPUTS: the fan P-Q and power
# curves, and the SimScale figures the alpha/beta coefficients were digitised from.
!docs/**/*.png
!docs/**/*.svg
# Likewise `*.flp` is ignored as generated and `examples/*/outputs` excludes the whole
# directory -- but git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded directory, so the
# directory has to be un-excluded first. The N-core floorplans take up to an hour each to
# build and the studies reference them by name, and 3000+ .flp files here are already
# tracked, so this directory is meant to be under version control.
!examples/floorplans/outputs/
!examples/floorplans/outputs/**

# --- Leakage calibration: keep the fit, drop the raw McPAT sweep ------------
# leakage_calibration.json is an INPUT to every study that loads a calibrated model.
# The mcpat_T*.xml/txt it was fitted from are regenerable via
# examples/calibrate_leakage_model.py and add ~2 MB of noise.
leakage_calibration/*
!leakage_calibration/leakage_calibration.json

# --- Compiled benchmark binary ----------------------------------------------
# examples/linpack is a 64-bit ELF built elsewhere; rebuild or fetch it rather than
# versioning a binary blob.
examples/linpack

# --- Personal scratch --------------------------------------------------------
runit.sh

# Stacks rendered on demand from spec strings; regenerate rather than commit.
HotGauge/HotGauge/thermal/stack_templates/_generated/
